2	/**
3	 * watch_for_stop.ts — Poll an issue/PR for a stop request and, when one arrives,
4	 * create the file `atoma run --stop-file` is watching.
5	 *
6	 * Runs in the background for the length of the agent step and is killed with it.
7	 *
8	 * ## Why polling
9	 *
10	 * A stop is decided outside the job, and nothing outside a job can write into that
11	 * job's filesystem. Something inside has to go and look. GitHub has no push channel
12	 * a running job can subscribe to, so this is the only shape available, and its cost
13	 * is one API request per interval — around 110 for a full-length run.
14	 *
15	 * ## Why it only looks at requests newer than the run
16	 *
17	 * A stop from last week is not a stop of this run. Without the cutoff, an issue that
18	 * was ever stopped could never be worked on again: every run would find the old
19	 * request on its first poll and stop before doing

